IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ira-dates`
IMPORT `ira-core`
IMPORT `ira-seat`

-- Industrial Relations Act 1996 (NSW) -- cases for the seat of the employee bringing the claim (ira-seat.l4). Every
-- expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (the section is named on each group), never copied from
-- the encoding's output; day counts are shown where they matter. Edges: the 21st day after the dismissal and the 22nd,
-- across a year end; the s 85(2) 21 days after a Commonwealth withdrawal; the 28th day after notice in a leap and a
-- common February; the 12-month and 15-month s 108B days from a 31st; the sixth anniversary of a 29 February; the
-- $62,200, $200,000 and $10,000 figures exactly and a dollar over; a package for part of a year taken over 12 months;
-- a 6-month increment deferral and 7; a 6-month fixed term and 5; a 3-month probation and 4.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the employee bringing the claim`

`ANY` MEANS `the date` 1 1 2000
`OTHER` MEANS `someone other than my spouse, de facto partner or parent`
`DISM` MEANS `I was dismissed`

`P6YES` MEANS `yes: Part 6 applies, and you may apply to the Industrial Relations Commission for your claim that the dismissal is harsh, unreasonable or unjust to be dealt with (ss 83, 84(1)); an industrial organisation of employees may apply for you (s 84(2))`
`P6FAMILY` MEANS `no: you are not an employee under this Act, because a person employed or engaged by their spouse, de facto partner or parent is not one (s 5(4))`
`P6NOTEMP` MEANS `no: you are not an employee under this Act: an employee means a person employed in an industry, or a person Schedule 1 deems an employee (s 5(1))`
`P6APP` MEANS `no: Part 6 does not apply to the dismissal of an apprentice or trainee (other than an existing worker trainee) (s 83(3))`
`P6SENIOR` MEANS `no: Part 6 does not apply to the dismissal of a Department Secretary, a Public Service senior executive or a police executive officer (s 83(3))`
`P6REG` MEANS `no: Part 6 does not apply to an employee a regulation exempts from it (s 83(2))`
`P6FED` MEANS `no: Part 6 does not apply, because you were employed under a Federal award and can apply (or but for an exclusion could apply) to the Fair Work Commission about this dismissal (s 83(1A))`
`P6HIGH` MEANS `no: Part 6 does not apply to an employee whose conditions are not set by an industrial instrument and whose annual remuneration is above the threshold (s 83(1)(b))`
`P6SILENT` MEANS `this Act does not say: dismissal includes dispensing with services and annulling an appointment for a public sector employee (s 83(5)(b)), and is silent for other employees`
`P6NODISM` MEANS `no: Part 6 deals with a dismissal (including the threat of one), and you were neither dismissed nor threatened (ss 83(5), 84(1))`
`P6NOCLAIM` MEANS `no: Part 6 deals with an employee's claim that the dismissal is harsh, unreasonable or unjust, and you do not make that claim (s 84(1))`

§§ `s 5 and s 83: does Part 6 apply`

-- Arguments: employed, Schedule 1, engaged by, public sector, apprentice, senior office, regulation exempts, Federal award, Fair Work Commission, instrument sets conditions, annual remuneration, regulation threshold?, threshold, what happened, claims harsh.
-- An award-covered private employee on $150,000: the income test applies only without an instrument (s 83(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 150000 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6YES`
-- No instrument: $62,200 exactly is not "greater than" $62,200; $62,201 is.
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 62200 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6YES`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 62201 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6HIGH`
-- A prescribed greater amount: $90,000 lets $80,000 (and $90,000) in; $70,000 does not; a lower figure ($50,000) is not "greater", so $62,200 stands.
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 80000 TRUE 90000 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6YES`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 90000 TRUE 90000 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6YES`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 80000 TRUE 70000 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6HIGH`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 62201 TRUE 50000 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6HIGH`
-- A public sector employee: no income test (s 83(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6YES`
-- s 5(4), s 5(1), Schedule 1.
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `my parent` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6FAMILY`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `my spouse or de facto partner` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6FAMILY`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` FALSE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6NOTEMP`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` FALSE TRUE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6YES`
-- s 83(3), s 83(2).
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 40000 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6APP`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 300000 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6SENIOR`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6REG`
-- s 83(1A): a Federal award employee who can go to the Fair Work Commission is out; one who cannot (and could not but for an exclusion) is in.
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6FED`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `DISM` TRUE EQUALS `P6YES`
-- s 83(5): a threat is a dismissal; dispensing with services is one for a public sector employee; the Act is silent for others.
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `I was threatened with dismissal` TRUE EQUALS `P6YES`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `my services were dispensed with or my appointment annulled` TRUE EQUALS `P6YES`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `my services were dispensed with or my appointment annulled` TRUE EQUALS `P6SILENT`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `I was neither dismissed nor threatened with dismissal` TRUE EQUALS `P6NODISM`
#ASSERT `Can I bring an unfair dismissal claim` TRUE FALSE `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 `DISM` FALSE EQUALS `P6NOCLAIM`

§§ `s 85: the time for applying`

`T85IN` MEANS `in time: the application was made not later than 21 days after the dismissal (s 85(1))`
`T85STILL` MEANS `still in time: you have not applied yet, and 21 days after the dismissal have not passed (s 85(1))`
`T85MUST` MEANS `out of time, but the Commission must accept it: you made a similar application under Commonwealth law in time, it was not settled or determined, and this application is (or, made today, would be) made within 21 days after that one was withdrawn or declined because of the remedy under Part 6 (s 85(2))`
`T85MAY` MEANS `out of time: more than 21 days after the dismissal; the Commission may accept it only if it considers there is a sufficient reason, having regard to the reason for and length of the delay, the hardship to you or the employer, and the employer's conduct (s 85(3))`

-- Dismissed 1 March 2025: 1 + 21 = 22 March 2025. Dismissed 15 December 2025: 15 + 21 = 36, less 31, is 5 January 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `the date` 22 3 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 15 12 2025) EQUALS `the date` 5 1 2026
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`the date` 22 3 2025) `ANY` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `ANY` EQUALS `T85IN`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`the date` 23 3 2025) `ANY` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `ANY` EQUALS `T85MAY`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 22 3 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `ANY` EQUALS `T85STILL`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 23 3 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `ANY` EQUALS `T85MAY`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 15 12 2025) TRUE (`the date` 5 1 2026) `ANY` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `ANY` EQUALS `T85IN`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 15 12 2025) TRUE (`the date` 6 1 2026) `ANY` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `ANY` EQUALS `T85MAY`
-- s 85(2): a Commonwealth application made in time and withdrawn on 1 May 2025: 1 + 21 = 22 May 2025.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`the date` 22 5 2025) `ANY` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 5 2025) EQUALS `T85MUST`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`the date` 23 5 2025) `ANY` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 5 2025) EQUALS `T85MAY`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 10 5 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 5 2025) EQUALS `T85MUST`
-- s 85(2) fails if the Commonwealth application was late, settled or determined, or neither withdrawn nor declined.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`the date` 10 5 2025) `ANY` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 5 2025) EQUALS `T85MAY`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`the date` 10 5 2025) `ANY` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 5 2025) EQUALS `T85MAY`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my dismissal` (`the date` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`the date` 10 5 2025) `ANY` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `ANY` EQUALS `T85MAY`

§§ `ss 89, 90: what the Commission may order`

-- Arguments: the Commission's view, another law gives redress, started there, lodged undertaking, 6 months' pay, leave shortfall, pay lost to reinstatement.
#ASSERT `What can the Commission order for my dismissal` `reinstatement is practicable` FALSE FALSE FALSE 40000 0 12000 EQUALS `reinstatement (s 89(1)), with pay for the time lost of at most` 12000
#ASSERT `What can the Commission order for my dismissal` `reinstatement is impracticable, but re-employment in another suitable position is practicable` FALSE FALSE FALSE 40000 0 12000 EQUALS `re-employment in another suitable position (s 89(2)), with pay for the time lost of at most` 12000
-- s 89(5): 6 months' pay $40,000; with $5,000 unpaid on leave without full pay counted as if paid, $45,000.
#ASSERT `What can the Commission order for my dismissal` `reinstatement and re-employment are both impracticable` FALSE FALSE FALSE 40000 0 12000 EQUALS `compensation of at most (s 89(5))` 40000
#ASSERT `What can the Commission order for my dismissal` `reinstatement and re-employment are both impracticable` FALSE FALSE FALSE 40000 5000 12000 EQUALS `compensation of at most (s 89(5))` 45000
-- s 90: another law's redress bars a s 89 order unless no proceedings were started there and an undertaking was lodged.
#ASSERT `What can the Commission order for my dismissal` `reinstatement and re-employment are both impracticable` TRUE TRUE FALSE 40000 0 0 EQUALS `no order under s 89: another law gives you redress for the dismissal, and you have started proceedings under it or have not lodged a written undertaking not to proceed under it (s 90)`
#ASSERT `What can the Commission order for my dismissal` `reinstatement is practicable` TRUE FALSE FALSE 40000 0 12000 EQUALS `no order under s 89: another law gives you redress for the dismissal, and you have started proceedings under it or have not lodged a written undertaking not to proceed under it (s 90)`
#ASSERT `What can the Commission order for my dismissal` `reinstatement is practicable` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40000 0 12000 EQUALS `no order under s 89: another law gives you redress for the dismissal, and you have started proceedings under it or have not lodged a written undertaking not to proceed under it (s 90)`
#ASSERT `What can the Commission order for my dismissal` `reinstatement and re-employment are both impracticable` TRUE FALSE TRUE 40000 0 0 EQUALS `compensation of at most (s 89(5))` 40000

§§ `ss 91-99: may I appeal against the decision`

`DAYES` MEANS `yes: you may appeal to the Industrial Relations Commission against the decision (s 98(1)), on any ground including that it was a detrimental action offence under the Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (s 98(2))`
`DISMISS` MEANS `to dismiss me (including dispensing with my services)`
`PROB` MEANS `no: an employee serving a probation or qualifying period fixed in advance at 3 months or less, or at a longer reasonable period, cannot appeal against annulment, dismissal or a direction to resign (s 98(3)(b))`
`CASUAL` MEANS `no: an employee engaged on a casual basis for a short period, not regular and systematic for 6 months with a reasonable expectation of continuing, cannot appeal against annulment, dismissal or a direction to resign (s 98(3)(c))`

-- Arguments: public sector, decision, instrument excludes, specified period/task, its months, probation, fixed in advance, probation months, longer one reasonable, casual short, regular 6 months, expectation, elected to forgo, other proceedings.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `DISMISS` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DAYES`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` FALSE `DISMISS` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: Part 7 appeals are for public sector employees (s 91, s 98(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `another decision` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the decision is not one of the appealable decisions listed in s 97(1)`
-- s 97(1)(a): "in excess of 6 months": 6 is not, 7 is.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE (`to defer payment of an increment` 6) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a deferral of an increment is appealable only if it is for more than 6 months (s 97(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE (`to defer payment of an increment` 7) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DAYES`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `DISMISS` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an award, enterprise agreement or other instrument or arrangement excludes your class from appealing to the Commission (s 92(1))`
-- s 98(3)(a): "less than 6 months": 5 is, 6 is not; and it reaches only (d), (f), (g) decisions, not a fine.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `DISMISS` FALSE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an employee engaged for a specified period or task of less than 6 months cannot appeal against annulment, dismissal or a direction to resign (s 98(3)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `DISMISS` FALSE TRUE 6 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DAYES`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `to impose a fine or forfeit pay` FALSE TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DAYES`
-- s 98(3)(b): fixed at 3 months is caught; 4 months only if reasonable; a probation not fixed in advance is not caught.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `DISMISS` FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `PROB`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `to annul my appointment on probation` FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE 4 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `PROB`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `DISMISS` FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DAYES`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `DISMISS` FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DAYES`
-- s 98(3)(c): a short casual is caught unless regular and systematic for 6 months with a reasonable expectation of continuing.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `to direct or require me to resign` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `CASUAL`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `DISMISS` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `CASUAL`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `DISMISS` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DAYES`
-- s 99(2).
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `to reduce my rank, classification, position, grade or pay` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: you elected in writing to forgo your s 98 appeal against this decision (s 99(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against my employer's decision` TRUE `to suspend me as a punishment for misconduct or a breach of a law, rule or direction` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: you have appealed or brought other proceedings about this decision elsewhere, or they were brought for you (s 99(2)(b))`

§§ `s 100B: the time for appealing`

`T100IN` MEANS `in time: the notice of appeal was lodged within 28 days after you were notified of the decision (s 100B(2))`
`T100STILL` MEANS `still in time: you have not lodged a notice of appeal yet, and 28 days after you were notified of the decision have not passed (s 100B(2))`
`T100LATE` MEANS `out of time: a notice of appeal must be lodged within 28 days after you are notified of the decision (s 100B(2)), and Part 7 gives the Commission no power to accept a late one`

-- Notified 10 February 2025: 10 + 28 = 38, less 28 (February 2025), is 10 March 2025. In 2024 (29 days): 9 March 2024.
#ASSERT `By when must I lodge my disciplinary appeal` (`the date` 10 2 2025) EQUALS `the date` 10 3 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I lodge my disciplinary appeal` (`the date` 10 2 2024) EQUALS `the date` 9 3 2024
#ASSERT `Am I in time to lodge my disciplinary appeal` (`the date` 10 2 2025) TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `T100IN`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to lodge my disciplinary appeal` (`the date` 10 2 2025) TRUE (`the date` 11 3 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `T100LATE`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to lodge my disciplinary appeal` (`the date` 10 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2024) `ANY` EQUALS `T100LATE`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to lodge my disciplinary appeal` (`the date` 10 2 2025) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 10 3 2025) EQUALS `T100STILL`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to lodge my disciplinary appeal` (`the date` 10 2 2025) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 11 3 2025) EQUALS `T100LATE`

§§ `s 105: is the contract unfair`

-- Arguments: industrial instrument, unfair/harsh/unconscionable, public interest, remuneration under it, an employee's pay, avoids an instrument.
#ASSERT `Is my contract an unfair contract` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: an industrial instrument is not a contract for Part 9 (s 105(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my contract an unfair contract` FALSE TRUE FALSE 60000 60000 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the contract is unfair, harsh or unconscionable (s 105(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my contract an unfair contract` FALSE FALSE TRUE 60000 60000 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the contract is against the public interest (s 105(1)(b))`
-- s 105(1)(c): "less than": $59,999 against $60,000 is; $60,000 against $60,000 is not.
#ASSERT `Is my contract an unfair contract` FALSE FALSE FALSE 59999 60000 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the contract provides a total remuneration less than an employee performing the work would receive (s 105(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Is my contract an unfair contract` FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 60000 FALSE EQUALS `no: an unfair contract means one that is unfair, harsh or unconscionable, against the public interest, underpays against an employee doing the work, or avoids an industrial instrument, and on these facts the contract is none of them (s 105(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my contract an unfair contract` FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 60000 TRUE EQUALS `yes: the contract is designed to avoid, or does avoid, the provisions of an industrial instrument (s 105(1)(d))`

§§ `ss 106, 108, 108A, 109A: may I apply`

`UCYES` MEANS `yes: you may apply to the Commission in Court Session for an order declaring the contract wholly or partly void, or varying it (ss 106, 108)`
`UCCAP` MEANS `no: no application can be made about a contract of employment whose remuneration package over the 12 months before the application (or the termination) exceeds the remuneration cap (s 108A(1))`
`MYPARTY` MEANS `I am a party to the contract`

-- Arguments: my place, instrument, work in an industry, related or collateral, contract of employment, unfair dismissal reason, package, months covered, partner with partners, profit share, regulation cap?, cap.
-- A contractor (not an employee): no cap applies to the package (s 108A(1) is about contracts of employment).
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 500000 12 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `UCYES`
-- An employee: $200,000 does not "exceed"; $200,001 does.
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 200000 12 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `UCYES`
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 200001 12 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `UCCAP`
-- s 108A(1)(b): $100,000 over 6 months is $200,000 over 12 (not over the cap); $100,001 is $200,002 (over).
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 100000 6 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `UCYES`
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 100001 6 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `UCCAP`
-- A prescribed greater cap ($250,000) lets $220,000 in; a lower figure is not "greater", so $200,000 stands.
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 220000 12 FALSE 0 TRUE 250000 EQUALS `UCYES`
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 220000 12 FALSE 0 TRUE 150000 EQUALS `UCCAP`
-- s 108A(2): a partner's profit share of $250,000 bars; $200,000 does not.
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 12 TRUE 250000 FALSE 0 EQUALS `no: a partner cannot apply about a contract with the other partners if the partner's profit share over the 12 months before the application (or the termination) exceeds the cap (s 108A(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 12 TRUE 200000 FALSE 0 EQUALS `UCYES`
-- s 108 and s 105(1).
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `I am not a party to the contract` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 50000 12 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `no: only a party (or would-be party), or the industrial organisations and associations s 108 names, may apply (s 108, "and not otherwise")`
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `I would be a party to the contract but for an order` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 50000 12 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `UCYES`
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 50000 12 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `no: an industrial instrument is not a contract for Part 9 (s 105(1))`
-- s 106(1), (2A).
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 50000 12 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `UCYES`
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 50000 12 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `no: the order is for a contract whereby a person performs work in an industry, or a related condition or collateral arrangement where the work is a significant purpose of the arrangements (s 106(1), (2A))`
-- s 109A reaches contracts of employment only.
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 50000 12 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `no: Division 2 does not apply where the contract of employment is said to be unfair for a reason for which an unfair dismissal application has been or could have been made under Part 6, or could have been but for s 83 (s 109A)`
#ASSERT `Can I apply about my unfair contract` `MYPARTY` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 12 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `UCYES`

§§ `s 108B: the time for applying`

`T108IN` MEANS `in time: the application was made not later than 12 months after the termination of the contract (s 108B(1))`
`T108EXC` MEANS `out of time, but within the further 3 months: the Commission may accept it only if you satisfy it that there are exceptional circumstances justifying the late application (s 108B(3))`
`T108BAR` MEANS `too late: more than 15 months after the termination, and the Commission has no jurisdiction to extend the time or accept the application (s 108B(2), (3))`

-- Terminated 31 August 2024: 12 months is 31 August 2025; 3 months after that is 30 November 2025 (November has 30 days).
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my unfair contract` FALSE `ANY` TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2030) `ANY` EQUALS `no time limit: the Act fixes a time only for a contract that has been terminated (s 108B(1))`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my unfair contract` TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2024) TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `T108IN`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my unfair contract` TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 9 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `T108EXC`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my unfair contract` TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2024) TRUE (`the date` 30 11 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `T108EXC`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my unfair contract` TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 12 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `T108BAR`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my unfair contract` TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2024) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `still in time: you have not applied yet, and 12 months after the termination have not passed (s 108B(1))`
-- Terminated 29 February 2024: 12 months is 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my unfair contract` TRUE (`the date` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 28 2 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `T108IN`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about my unfair contract` TRUE (`the date` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `T108EXC`

§§ `ss 210, 213: victimisation`

`VYES` MEANS `yes: you are presumed to have been victimised because of the matter you allege, and the employer or organisation has not satisfied the Commission that it was not a substantial and operative cause; you may apply for orders under s 213 (s 210(2))`
`UNION` MEANS `I am or was a union member or official, or an elected representative of employees`
`POL` MEANS `I engaged, or proposed to engage, in public or political activity`

-- Arguments: employee or job applicant, detriment from their action, reason, activity interferes, rebutted.
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE TRUE `UNION` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VYES`
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE TRUE `I complained that a workplace matter is unsafe or a risk to health, or exercised work health and safety consultation functions` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VYES`
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE TRUE `UNION` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the presumption is rebutted, because the employer or organisation satisfied the Commission that the matter you allege was not a substantial and operative cause of the detrimental action (s 210(2))`
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` FALSE TRUE `UNION` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 210 does not reach this: it protects an employee or prospective employee`
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE TRUE `another reason` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 210 does not reach this: the reason you allege is not one of those s 210(1) lists`
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE TRUE `POL` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: public or political activity is protected unless it interferes with the performance of your duties, and yours does (s 210(1)(h))`
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE TRUE `POL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VYES`
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE FALSE `UNION` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say: the s 210(2) presumption arises only where you suffered a detriment as a result of the employer's or organisation's action, and "victimise" is not defined`

-- Contravention 20 June 2025: 20 + 21 = 41, less 30 (June), is 11 July 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply about victimisation` (`the date` 20 6 2025) EQUALS `the date` 11 7 2025
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about victimisation` (`the date` 20 6 2025) TRUE (`the date` 11 7 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `in time: the application was made within 21 days after the contravention (s 213(3))`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about victimisation` (`the date` 20 6 2025) TRUE (`the date` 12 7 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `out of time: more than 21 days after the contravention; the Commission may accept it only if it considers there is a sufficient reason, having regard to the reason for and length of the delay, the hardship to you or the other party, and the conduct complained of (s 213(4))`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply about victimisation` (`the date` 20 6 2025) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 1 7 2025) EQUALS `still in time: you have not applied yet, and 21 days after the contravention have not passed (s 213(3))`

§§ `ss 365-369, 379: recovering money`

`AWARD` MEANS `an amount payable under an industrial instrument, or long service leave or annual holiday pay under the Acts s 364(2) names`
`ME` MEANS `I apply myself`
`R365` MEANS `yes: an industrial court may order your employer to pay the unpaid amount (s 365)`
`R6Y` MEANS `no: an application may be made only for money that became due within the 6 years immediately before it (s 369(3))`

-- Arguments: kind, who applies, day it fell due, applied, day applied, today.
-- Due 15 July 2019: the sixth anniversary is 15 July 2025 (fork F3). Due 29 February 2016: 28 February 2022.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to recover money` (`the date` 15 7 2019) EQUALS `the date` 15 7 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to recover money` (`the date` 29 2 2016) EQUALS `the date` 28 2 2022
#ASSERT `Can I recover the money I am owed` `AWARD` `ME` (`the date` 15 7 2019) TRUE (`the date` 15 7 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `R365`
#ASSERT `Can I recover the money I am owed` `AWARD` `ME` (`the date` 15 7 2019) TRUE (`the date` 16 7 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `R6Y`
#ASSERT `Can I recover the money I am owed` `AWARD` `ME` (`the date` 29 2 2016) TRUE (`the date` 28 2 2022) `ANY` EQUALS `R365`
#ASSERT `Can I recover the money I am owed` `AWARD` `ME` (`the date` 29 2 2016) TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2022) `ANY` EQUALS `R6Y`
#ASSERT `Can I recover the money I am owed` `AWARD` `ME` (`the date` 15 7 2019) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 1 1 2025) EQUALS `R365`
#ASSERT `Can I recover the money I am owed` `AWARD` `ME` (`the date` 15 7 2019) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 1 8 2025) EQUALS `R6Y`
#ASSERT `Can I recover the money I am owed` `an amount payable under my contract of employment, where an industrial instrument fixes the minimum rate for the work` `ME` (`the date` 1 1 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `yes: an industrial court may order your employer to pay the unpaid amount under your contract (s 366)`
#ASSERT `Can I recover the money I am owed` `an amount payable under my contract of employment, where no industrial instrument fixes the minimum rate for the work` `ME` (`the date` 1 1 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `no: s 366 applies only if an industrial instrument fixes the minimum rate or amount of remuneration for the work (s 366(2)); you may still sue for the money as a debt in another court`
#ASSERT `Can I recover the money I am owed` `pay for work whose rate no industrial instrument fixes for me, though one fixes it for others (or for my other work with the same employer)` `ME` (`the date` 1 1 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `yes, if the industrial court is satisfied that it is just and equitable for the employer to pay you for the work: it fixes an appropriate rate and may order payment (s 367)`
#ASSERT `Can I recover the money I am owed` `superannuation contributions an industrial instrument requires my employer to make` `an inspector, a Public Service agency employee or a union officer applies for me, with my written consent` (`the date` 1 1 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `yes: an industrial court may order your employer to restore you, as far as practicable, to the position you would be in had the contributions been made, including paying the unpaid contributions and their earnings to the fund (s 368)`
#ASSERT `Can I recover the money I am owed` `AWARD` `someone else applies for me without my written consent` (`the date` 1 1 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2025) `ANY` EQUALS `no: someone else may apply for you only with your written consent, and only an inspector, a Public Service agency employee or an officer of an industrial organisation (s 369(1)(b))`

-- s 379(3): $10,000 is within; $10,001 is capped; a prescribed other amount (higher or lower) replaces it.
#ASSERT `How much can a small claims order give me` 8000 FALSE 0 EQUALS `the whole amount claimed is within the small claims maximum, so a small claims order may be for all of it (s 379(3))`
#ASSERT `How much can a small claims order give me` 10000 FALSE 0 EQUALS `the whole amount claimed is within the small claims maximum, so a small claims order may be for all of it (s 379(3))`
#ASSERT `How much can a small claims order give me` 10001 FALSE 0 EQUALS `a small claims order for you can be at most` 10000
#ASSERT `How much can a small claims order give me` 15000 TRUE 20000 EQUALS `the whole amount claimed is within the small claims maximum, so a small claims order may be for all of it (s 379(3))`
#ASSERT `How much can a small claims order give me` 8000 TRUE 5000 EQUALS `a small claims order for you can be at most` 5000
